# Owner preferences (Idle Party)

Source: owner answers (vibe-coder). Agents follow these without re-asking.
Last preference sync: **2026-08-22** (work loop: AL20 save, large independent
batches, owner plays their AL20 save; APK only when they ask; short “what to
test” then wait. Play Alpha fact still **1.12.68 / 97**; no IAP. Other product locks
unchanged).

## Near-term focus

- **Default roadmap:** 90-day M1–M3 shipped. Operate from `docs/CONTENT_CADENCE.md`
  — balance + one player-visible slice + What’s New + decision table (kits before
  new specs). Don’t invent a competing list. **Now:** **AL20 hub + dungeon feel**
  so the owner’s save always knows what to chase — not new zones, not new classes.
- Vague “gör spelet bättre / vad härnäst” → **AL20 hub + dungeon** (chase
  clarity, wipe advice the game can prove, dead menu chrome). Not first-hour
  onboarding, not a new dungeon or spec, not `/init` / cleanup / CI chores.
  First-hour systems may stay for new players; they are not the default work.
- Prefer **game feel / content** over Play ops busywork (closed-test recruitment can idle in background).
- Play production remains a goal, but day-to-day work defaults to **content + feel** unless the owner asks about Play.
- Background why (optional read): `docs/TOP_GAMES_RESEARCH.md`.

## Distribution

- Goal: **Google Play “for real” soon** (not sideload-only forever).
- Prefer work that unblocks Play when touching store: CI signing secrets, closed-test 12×14, production access — see `docs/PLAY_STORE.md`.
- **Current fact:** GitHub Releases (APK/AAB) is still the primary install path. Play Console app `com.idleparty.app` exists (listing + closed Alpha, last submit **1.12.68 / 97**, 2026-08-27; testers may still be on **1.12.60 / 90** until review publishes). Working ship is **1.12.70**. **Production is not live**. Optional Play Games (META → SETTINGS) is opt-in, not a store blocker.
- **Platforms now:** Android (+ existing web playtest tooling OK). **No iOS** and **no shipping web as a product** for now.

## UI target device (mandatory)

- **Phone-only product.** Design and ship for portrait phones (~360–430 CSS px wide). Do not optimize for desktop/tablet layouts as the real product.
- **Owner reference phone: Samsung Galaxy A56** (1080×2340 @ DPR 3 → **360×780** CSS). Cursor browser playtest must always emulate this (or equivalent 360-wide portrait) via CDP device metrics — never judge UI at desktop/tablet width.
- Hub, GEAR/BAG, menus, tooltips, touch targets: assume **finger + portrait**. Hover-only UX is playtest-only; phone must work with tap / long-press.
- Flutter **web** remains a Cursor playtest harness with **forced phone emulation** — never treat wide desktop chrome as the shipping UI.
- **Owner play notes win.** They play **their own AL20 save** on the A56
  (~60+ min/week). Hub “am I doing the right thing?” notes, wipe notes, and
  unused-menu notes *are* the batch. No tester telemetry yet — do not wait on
  closed testers. Don’t invent a 10-minute browser pass instead of their phone.

## Work style

- Prefer **large batches** the agent can finish alone (including ~1h
  autonomous passes). Few check-ins mid-batch.
- Verify with analyze/tests (and hub smoke if UI) **before** handing notes
  to the owner.
- **Loop:** build → verify with analyze/tests → **≤5 lines: what
  changed / what to look for** → **wait**. Do **not** build or copy a
  sideload APK unless the owner **explicitly** asks for one. Do not write
  essays. Do not GitHub-release or upload Play AAB until they answered.
- **Then** (after they OK play notes **and** asked for a build): ship both
  GitHub APK/AAB **and** Play Alpha. Testers never get a build before the
  owner has played it.
- **Commit locally** when analyze/tests are green so work is not lost. Don’t
  wait for “ska jag commita?”. Still **ask** before push / PR / tag / Play.
  Never force-push or skip hooks unless they say so in that turn.
- **Code shape:** prefer splitting a giant file (`game_logic`, `spatial_combat`,
  …) when a change needs a home. Do **not** merge more into those files.
  `is2_shell` is already thin — new HUD goes in `lib/ui/shell/`. Keep
  SpatialCombat as combat authority (extract helpers, don’t add a second fight
  sim).
- **Dead code:** delete unused files/APIs with zero callers. Keep JSON/save
  fields that old saves may still contain (`save-migrate`). Unused
  `@Deprecated` helpers that are not serialized may go.
- **Git:** daily work on `main`. `release/x.y.z` only when cutting a tag. Don’t open a release branch for chores.
- **Don’t stage** `windows/flutter/generated_*` unless `pubspec.yaml` plugins actually changed (`jni` noise from `pub get` is not a product change).
- **Product locks stay** (phone, English UI, fairness, no IAP, cadence after
  90d M1–M3, legal/Kenney). Agents may tighten *workstyle* so they can finish;
  they must not weaken those locks. Cursor/AI safety (no exploits, no foreign
  dumps) is not overridable from this file.

## Game feel & fantasy

- **Owner lens is endgame (AL20).** Hub must make “what do I do next?”
  obvious on that save. Progression / power still matters; first-hour stays
  calm for new players but is not the default polish target.
- Keep hub/UI **readable and low-panic** (not sweaty esports chrome).
- After **2 wipes on the same floor**, dungeon may suggest a FORGE fix **only
  if the sim knows the deficit** (e.g. ATK vs DEF vs wrong zone). Bag /
  floor-too-far / early DEF / MARKET may fire on wipe 1. No guessed tips.
  Show it **in the dungeon**, not after they are already back in hub.
- **Dead chrome the owner tried and does not use — hide or remove, don’t
  polish:** BAG **Scrap**, **Sell junk**, GEAR **Sell**, **Loadouts**. Keep
  save fields if old saves still have them.
- **Early game:** approachable. **Endgame** (high AL / Gauntlet / late zones): OK to be **competitive / grindy**.

## Content priorities

- **Kits:** polish what exists (fairness + clarity + fantasy) before adding many new specs. **No new classes/specs** until the owner revisits.
- **Zones:** **no new zones for now.** Identity polish of existing floors is OK if it serves feel; do not start dungeon #16 unless asked.
- **Feel / retention:** make the loop they already have (fight → loot → level → claim) punchier and more readable so a short phone session wants “one more floor.”
- **Meta loops** (daily vault / Will / Gauntlet / season): push toward **“I always know what I’m chasing today”** — hub TODAY with READY/ALMOST, Ascend Blessing + unlock teasers, clear claims.
- **God Hand:** owner undecided (fun steer vs deeper strategy) — don’t redesign GH direction without asking.
- **Monetization:** **no IAP / no paid store** for now. Optional hub **POWERUPS**
  rewarded ads (1 finished ad = 3 hours of ×2 gold + 25% ATK, stack time up to
  24h). Ads never interrupt combat. Still no paid shop unless the owner asks.

## Language

- **In-game copy stays English** (UI, tips, What’s New, guides).
- Agent ↔ owner chat: plain Swedish (or their language). After a coding pass:
  what to test on the phone, then wait. No jargon quizzes.

## Balance vs fantasy

**Owner choice: fairness first (rättvisa först).**

When a kit is fun but share/CI says HIGH (or clearly stomps peers):

1. Trim until live-light gate / ±20% share band is honest — fantasy second.
2. Keep *identity* if possible (names, VFX, rotation shape) but numbers must come in line.
3. Plain Swedish one-liner when done: “för stark → sänkt så den matchar andra.”
4. Do **not** leave documented HIGH outliers “for flavor” without an explicit later override.

